{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Whoever has sinned against Me, I will erase him from My book.</b> Whoever has sinned against Me — I will erase his merits from My book, so that he may merit forgiveness of sin to counterbalance them. This has never been the case, for the law before Me is the opposite: each one bears the punishment of his sin and receives the reward of his merits, for a mitzvah does not extinguish a transgression — all the more so that I would not set your merits to their account."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:49.053653918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}